-- Part 1A.
#ASSERT `Can the person who hurt me be liable for not taking precautions` `as the injured person` `all three limbs found` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the person who hurt me be liable for not taking precautions` `as the injured person` `no limb found` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the person who hurt me be liable for not taking precautions` `as the injured person` `the risk found insignificant` EQUALS `yes if` (`Can they be liable for not taking precautions` `the risk found insignificant`)
#ASSERT `Am I presumed partly to blame because I was intoxicated` `as the injured person` TRUE `riding drunk` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I presumed partly to blame because I was intoxicated` `as the injured person` TRUE `drugged without knowing` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I presumed partly to blame because I was intoxicated` `as the injured person` TRUE `drunk, but proves it did not contribute` EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I presumed contributorily negligent` `drunk, but proves it did not contribute`)
#ASSERT `Will I be held partly to blame for my own injury` `as the injured person` `Jake doored on a delivery, the CTP Act applying` `Jake riding sober and with care` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Will I be held partly to blame for my own injury` `as the injured person` `Jake doored on a delivery, the CTP Act applying` `riding drunk` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Will I be held partly to blame for my own injury` `as the injured person` `a worker's common-law claim against the employer` `riding drunk` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Will I be held partly to blame for my own injury` `as the injured person` `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` `riding drunk` EQUALS `yes if` (`Will I be held contributorily negligent` `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` `riding drunk`)
#ASSERT `Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill mountain biking, after asking about the risk` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` `Jake's delivery riding` EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat my claim` `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` `Jake's delivery riding`)
#ASSERT `Does a risk warning defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` `a sign at the trail head, read by an adult rider` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does a risk warning defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` `a waiver form explained to the parent of a 15-year-old` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does a risk warning defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` `a sign read by a 17-year-old riding alone` EQUALS `yes if` (`Does a risk warning defeat my claim` `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` `a sign read by a 17-year-old riding alone`)
#ASSERT `Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away my claim` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away my claim` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away my claim` `as the injured person` TRUE `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the contract take away my claim` `the trail crash` `downhill, obvious` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been aware of the risk that injured me` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been aware of the risk that injured me` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been aware of the risk that injured me` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I presumed aware of the risk` `the trail crash` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Did the person who hurt me have to warn me of the risk` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no duty to warn me of an obvious risk (s 5O)`
#ASSERT `Did the person who hurt me have to warn me of the risk` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `s 5O does not take away a duty to warn; the general law decides`
#ASSERT `Did the person who hurt me have to warn me of the risk` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` (`Did they have to warn me` `the trail crash` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the inherent risk rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the inherent risk rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` `the trail crash` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the inherent risk rule defeat the claim I make` `as the injured person` `an assault meant to injure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the inherent risk rule defeat my claim` `an assault meant to injure` TRUE FALSE)

